course: dictionary
lesson: 11812
title: Bidders and offers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bidder is someone who makes a bid, which is an offer of money. When you read about an auction or a job that people compete for, look for bidders. They are the people trying to win.
explain: «Three bidders wanted the old painting, so the price kept going up.» The word so tells you the bidders were competing. Each one offered more money, and the price rose.
explain: Look at the words around bidder for clues. Highest bidder means the person who offers the most. Lowest bidder means the person who offers the smallest price, which is often used when people compete to do a job. Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A bidder is a person or company who makes a bid, an offer of money or a price.
fact: At an auction, the highest bidder wins and buys the item.
fact: When people bid to do building work, the lowest bidder offers the smallest price for the job.
fact: «Bidder» is built from the word «bid», so if you know bid, you can work out bidder.
fact: «Sold to the highest bidder» means the item went to the person who offered the most money.
exercise: «The painting was sold to the highest bidder.» What is a bidder? | A person who paints pictures for a gallery | A person who sells old things in a shop | A person who guards the auction room | *A person who offers money for something at an auction
exercise: «Five builders sent in offers to mend the school roof, and the council picked the lowest bidder.» What does lowest bidder mean? | The builder who arrived at the school last | *The builder who offered to do the job for the smallest price | The builder who was the shortest of the five | The builder who wore the oldest coat
exercise: Which word in «Three bidders wanted the old painting, so the price kept going up.» means people who make offers of money? | old | painting | price | *bidders
test: «The auction was busy, and every bidder wanted the vase.» What is the bidder doing? | *Offering money to buy the vase | Hiding the vase from the others | Cleaning the vase | Painting a picture of the vase
test: Which phrase means the person who offers the most money at an auction? | the oldest painting | the lowest bidder | the tallest builder | *the highest bidder
exam: Mum says, «The bidders at the car sale kept raising their offers until only one was left.» What does bidders mean? | People who drive the cars to the sale | People who check the cars for damage | *People who offer money to buy the car | People who sell cars at a garage
